WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.890
Speaker 1: Last night, Joe Biden delivered
his first speech to a joint session of Congress,

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.960
the Senate coming over to the House of Representatives
to hear Joe Biden deliver this speech, not

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.540
called the State of the Union.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.480
It's typically not called the State of the
Union when it's a president's first year in

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.790
office, but it is essentially a State of the
Union.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:23.890
And Joe Biden did lay out his plan for a one
point eight trillion dollar spending package,

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.660
including funding paid leave, community college
and all of the things we previewed in some

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.910
detail yesterday.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.629
So I won't redo the policy proposal nitty
gritty again.

00:00:34.629 --> 00:00:38.989
But it was overall a very policy heavy speech.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:44.030
This could not have been more different from
recent State of the Union addresses from Donald

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:51.929
Trump, which contained almost no policy but
Trump aside even compared to Barack Obama.

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:58.139
Compared to George W. Bush before him, it
was really just a focus on policy with very

00:00:58.139 --> 00:00:59.760
little vapid political rhetoric.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.659
Now, that's not necessarily good or bad.

00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:07.000
Vapid political rhetoric can be a good thing
if it's inspirational or coalesces people

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.280
or it can be nonsense or whatever.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.420
But this was really a focus on policy, a focus
on vaccination.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:22.060
Even Ted Cruz here applauding after Joe Biden
announces 220 million vaccine doses in 100

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.760
days and urges everybody to get themselves
vaccinated.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.810
Speaker 2: Right now, right away.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:31.040
Go get vaccinated, America.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:36.159
Go and get the vaccination there available.

00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:39.630
Eligible now.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:48.290
Speaker 1: Joe Biden talking about those vaccination
numbers, but also talking a lot about job

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:51.619
creation,
Speaker 2: all this is all going on, the economy

00:01:51.619 --> 00:02:04.240
creating more than one million, 300000 new
jobs and 100 days more jobs in the first.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:09.190
More jobs in the first 100 days than any president
on record.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:12.300
The International Monetary Fund.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:24.050
Speaker 1: To international now, of course,
that is true, context does matter.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:30.940
We were and are in a recovery period from
an externally motivated job loss caused by

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:31.940
the pandemic.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.480
Now, many of those jobs are coming back.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.211
You expect any president to brag about job
growth, whether or not they had a hand in

00:02:39.211 --> 00:02:40.670
it, it is still a good thing.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:43.160
But it is important to understand the context.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.410
Many of these jobs would be coming back regardless
of who was president.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.870
I'd rather it be Joe Biden than Donald Trump
for sure.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:55.350
Joe Biden then jumping right into talking
about the economy and talking about the importance

00:02:55.350 --> 00:03:01.280
of unions, much to Bernie Sanders delight
Speaker 2: and unions built the middle class.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:06.880
So that's why I'm calling on Congress.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:14.560
To pass, protect the right to organize, act,
the pro act and send it to my desk so we can

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.870
support the right to unionize.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:25.670
And by the way,
Speaker 1: and Joe Biden then, much to the

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:31.460
pleasure of most Democrats in the crowd, but
not Mitt Romney and Lauren Bobert and others

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:35.370
saying let's raise the minimum wage to fifteen
dollars an hour,

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:40.870
Speaker 2: let's raise the minimum wage to
15 dollars.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.150
No one.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:53.940
No one working 40 hours a week, no one working
40 hours a week should live below the poverty

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.270
line.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:59.800
We need to ensure greater equity and opportunity
for women while we're doing this.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.910
Let's get the Paycheck Fairness Act to my
desk as well.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:03.910
Equal pay.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.410
Spent much too long.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.900
And you wonder whether it's too long.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.620
Look behind
Speaker 1: you.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:16.290
Joe Biden also laying out how he will pay
for much of these ideas, saying the rich will

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.290
pay.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:20.780
And Mitt Romney didn't seem particularly thrilled
with that either.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:25.310
Speaker 2: And the wealthiest one percent
of Americans have just begun to pay their

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:36.430
fair share, just their fair share.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:41.280
Sometimes I have arguments with my friends
in the Democratic Party.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.870
I think you should be able to become a billionaire
and a millionaire, but pay your fair share.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:52.590
Speaker 1: And on economics, a moment that
many people liked, which got a lot of attention.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:57.670
Joe Biden saying straight up trickle down
economics has never worked.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:05.870
Speaker 2: My fellow Americans, trickle down,
trickle down economics has never worked this

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:12.300
time to grow the economy from the bottom in
the middle out.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:29.870
Speaker 1: Now, I love this because I already
planned later today to talk about Joe Biden

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:37.560
and biodynamics as they are being called,
as the antithesis to Reaganomics, that line

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.560
trickle down economics has never worked, is
actually part of it, saying it as directly

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.560
as anybody can.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.550
And we're going to come back to that in more
detail on foreign policy.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:51.770
Joe Biden pointing out that he's just getting
out of Afghanistan, something that Republicans

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:55.950
loved when it was Trump who announced that
Trump failed to do it.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:01.160
Joe Biden is doing it and Republicans are
no longer clapping about it.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:07.590
Speaker 2: And American leadership means ending
the forever war in Afghanistan.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:11.280
Unidentified: We have.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.730
We have.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:23.590
Speaker 2: Without hyperbole, the greatest
fighting force in the history of the world,

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:28.550
I'm the first president in 40 years who knows
what it means to have a son serving in a war

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:29.620
zone.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:34.650
Today, we have service members serving in
the same war zone as their parents did.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:40.360
We have service members in Afghanistan who
are not yet born on 9/11.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:46.389
The war in Afghanistan, as we remember, the
debates here were never meant to be multigenerational

00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:48.280
undertakings of nation building.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:52.050
Speaker 1: Of course, it was never really
about just getting out of Afghanistan.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.980
It was can we cheer for something Trump is
doing?

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.840
Biden now is actually going to do the thing.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:01.090
We cheered Trump for announcing, but we don't
share anymore because we are merely political

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:02.090
hypocrites.

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:06.030
Real quick, here is Senator Ted Cruz sleeping
during the speech.

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:12.870
He looked very, very sleepy, apparently dreaming
of Cancun and Joe Biden ultimately closing

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.770
out his speech.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:15.770
Take a listen to that.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:20.170
Speaker 2: It's never, ever, ever been a good
bet to bet against America.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.370
And it still isn't where the United States
of America.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:30.820
There's not a single thing, nothing, nothing
beyond our capacity.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:34.900
We can do whatever we set our minds to if
we do it together.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.730
So let's begin to get together.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:40.290
God bless you all and may God protect our
troops.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:43.650
Thank you for your patience.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:50.680
Speaker 1: Some of the people in the camp
of Biden is a weakling and he's old and senile

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:55.800
and demented, we're expecting a very short
speech and a very incoherent speech.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:01.460
Biden going much longer than recent presidents
have during their first joint addresses to

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.020
Congress and very coherent.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.420
I thought it was a well-written speech.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.180
I thought it was about the right duration.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.680
I often think things are too long.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.840
I think it was about the right duration.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:17.130
And now actually comes the tough part, which
is Joe Biden has laid out a variety of different

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.210
policy ideas.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:23.970
Can Joe Biden get any of what he proposed
done?

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:29.220
And that is certainly easier said than done
when not only do you have zero Republican

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:34.209
support in the House and Senate for anything
you want to do, but it's not even clear you

00:08:34.209 --> 00:08:37.519
have the support of all of the Democrats in
the Senate either.

00:08:37.519 --> 00:09:48.910
And we will talk about that is these proposals
become more formalized and start to be debated.

